":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"```suggestion\n\t\t\tThe hint string contains the number of flags to display, such as [code]\"8\"[/code] or [code]\"16\"[/code]. The first flag in the grid has value 1, the next 2, then 4, 8, 16, and so on.\n```\nPlease use [Oxford comma](https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/documentation/guidelines/docs_writing_guidelines.html#use-the-oxford-comma-to-enumerate-anything).","created_at":"2026-03-23T17:34:45Z","updated_at":"2026-03-23T17:36:12Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117715#discussion_r2976533860","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117715","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2976533860"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117715#discussion_r2976533860"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117715"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2976533860/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":3002,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":30,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2976536553","pull_request_review_id":3993438516,"id":2976536553,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6xalfp","diff_hunk":"@@ -3007,7 +2997,18 @@\n \t\t<constant name=\"PROPERTY_HINT_FILE_PATH\" value=\"44\" enum=\"PropertyHint\">\n \t\t\tLike [constant PROPERTY_HINT_FILE], but the property is stored as a raw path, not UID. That means the reference will be broken if you move the file. Consider using [constant PROPERTY_HINT_FILE] when possible.\n \t\t</constant>\n-\t\t<constant name=\"PROPERTY_HINT_MAX\" value=\"45\" enum=\"PropertyHint\">\n+\t\t<constant name=\"PROPERTY_HINT_FLAGS_GRID\" value=\"45\" enum=\"PropertyHint\">\n+\t\t\tHints that an [int] property is a bitmask with numbered bit flags, displayed in a compact grid.\n+\t\t\tThe hint string contains the number of flags to display, such as [code]\"8\"[/code] or [code]\"16\"[/code]. The first flag in the grid has value 1, the next 2, then 4, 8, 16 and so on.\n+\t\t\t[b]Note:[/b] A flag value must be at least [code]1[/code] and at most [code]2 ** 32 - 1[/code].\n+\t\t</constant>\n+\t\t<constant name=\"PROPERTY_HINT_FLAGS_GRID_NAMED\" value=\"46\" enum=\"PropertyHint\">\n+\t\t\tHints that an [int] property is a bitmask with named bit flags, displayed in a compact grid.\n+\t\t\tThe hint string is a comma separated list of names such as [code]\"Bit0,Bit1,Bit2,Bit3\"[/code]. Whitespace is [b]not[/b] removed from either end of a name. The first name in the list has value 1, the next 2, then 4, 8, 16 and so on. Explicit values can also be specified by appending [code]:integer[/code] to the name, e.g. [code]\"A:4,B:8,C:16\"[/code]. You can also combine several flags ([code]\"A:4,B:8,AB:12,C:16\"[/code]).","path":"doc/classes/@GlobalScope.xml","commit_id":"1c58d2c0a6ef24f5fdd1811bb9f8afac51f19daf","original_commit_id":"1c58d2c0a6ef24f5fdd1811bb9f8afac51f19daf","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"```suggestion\n\t\t\tThe hint string is a comma separated list of names such as [code]\"Bit0,Bit1,Bit2,Bit3\"[/code]. Whitespace is [b]not[/b] removed from either end of a name. The first name in the list has value 1, the next 2, then 4, 8, 16, and so on. Explicit values can also be specified by appending [code]:integer[/code] to the name, e.g. [code]\"A:4,B:8,C:16\"[/code]. You can also combine several flags ([code]\"A:4,B:8,AB:12,C:16\"[/code]).\n```","created_at":"2026-03-23T17:35:14Z","updated_at":"2026-03-23T17:36:12Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117715#discussion_r2976536553","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117715","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/commen